# The README fixtures pin exact bytes: a UTF-8 BOM and either LF or CRLF line
# endings. Git's `core.autocrlf` (on by default on Windows) would rewrite the
# LF fixtures to CRLF on checkout, so mark them binary and ship the working
# tree exactly as committed. The test checks the bytes before running doctor,
# which is what makes a BOM or line-ending regression visible.
readme-*/README.md -text
